  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Initially there are 20 micrograms of bacteria in a petri dish. After 4 minutes, there are 30 micrograms. Assuming the mass of bacteria is growing exponentially, determine the mass after 6 minutes, correct to the nearest microgram.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "37 micrograms.",
      "worked": "Let $M(t)$ be the mass in micrograms after $t$ minutes, with $M(t)=M_0b^{kt}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}M_0b^0&=20\\\\M_0&=20\\\\20b^{4k}&=30\\\\b^{4k}&=\\frac32\\\\4k&=\\log_b\\frac32\\\\k&=\\frac14\\log_b\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing $b^{\\log_b x}=x$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}M(t)&=20b^{\\frac{t}{4}\\log_b\\frac32}\\\\M(t)&=20\\left(b^{\\log_b\\frac32}\\right)^{t/4}\\\\M(t)&=20\\left(\\frac32\\right)^{t/4}\\\\M(6)&=20\\left(\\frac32\\right)^{6/4}\\\\M(6)&\\approx37\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe mass after 6 minutes is approximately 37 micrograms.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 88
  },
